Field Guide turns local observations into a reference that remains useful away
from a network connection. We worked across information architecture, visual
language, and offline storage.

= Finding the right specimen

The interface balances concise identification cues with illustrations and
seasonal notes. A compact taxonomy keeps browsing useful without requiring
specialist vocabulary.

= A durable field tool

The final design works on small phones in bright outdoor light and synchronizes
new observations only when a connection is available.
